.TH LAUNCHDX 1 "August 17, 2026" "launchdx 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
launchdx \- find out exactly why macOS blocked your app
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B launchdx
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.I target
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B launchdx
is a read only diagnostic CLI for modern Apple Silicon macOS systems. It
inspects an application bundle or a download container (.dmg or .pkg),
collects evidence from public Apple APIs and Apple provided tools, and
explains the most likely launch blocker. Disk images are mounted read only.
Installer packages are expanded into a temporary directory. The original
target is never modified.
.PP
launchdx does not modify the inspected application. It does not remove
quarantine attributes, change Gatekeeper settings, modify TCC databases,
disable system protections, re sign applications, or install certificates.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B diagnose
Inspect an application bundle, disk image, or installer package and produce a
diagnosis with findings, evidence, and suggested repairs.
.TP
.B evidence
Inspect an application bundle, disk image, or installer package and show the
raw evidence without the diagnosis summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a machine readable JSON report.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Include suggested repair actions in the text output.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable colored output.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage information.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Inspection completed without a confirmed launch blocker.
.TP
.B 1
A confirmed launch blocker was found.
.TP
.B 64
Command usage error.
.TP
.B 65
Target type is outside the supported .app, .dmg, and .pkg scope.
.TP
.B 66
Target path does not exist.
.TP
.B 69
Required security evidence is unavailable.
.TP
.B 70
Internal tool error.
.TP
.B 77
Inspection is limited by permissions.
.TP
.B 78
Configuration error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Diagnose an application:
.PP
.RS
.nf
launchdx diagnose /Applications/MyApp.app
.fi
.RE
.PP
Emit a JSON report:
.PP
.RS
.nf
launchdx diagnose /Applications/MyApp.app --json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show raw evidence:
.PP
.RS
.nf
launchdx evidence /Applications/MyApp.app
.fi
.RE
.SH SUPPORTED PLATFORM
Modern Apple Silicon macOS, macOS 13 or newer. Application bundles with the
\&.app extension are supported. Disk images (.dmg) and installer packages
(.pkg) are opened read only so the nested application can be diagnosed.
ZIP archives remain outside the current scope.
.SH SEE ALSO
